From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 20:54:58 -0647
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zumapro: Enable ramoops

The region stock uses for ramoops was only reserved, because zuma's
user-build bootloader doesn't keep it across a warm reset. zumapro's
does: on the Pixel 9a, after a hang that ended in a watchdog reset,
the console zone held the previous kernel's log up to the hang (after
the bootloader's own log, which it writes at the start of the zone).

Describe it as ramoops with stock zumapro's layout, which every other
Google board in this tree also uses: console-size 0x200000 and pmsg-size
0x200000, with no record-size, so the console zone starts where the
bootloader writes its log.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 .../boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-reserved-memory.dtsi  | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-reserved-memory.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-reserved-memory.dtsi
index 66157671c..c170f2422 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-reserved-memory.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-reserved-memory.dtsi
@@ -176,10 +176,17 @@ debug_kinfo_reserved: debug_kinfo_reserved@fd3fe000 {
 			no-map;
 		};
 
-		/* Reserve only; the pstore consumer is not enabled yet. */
+		/*
+		 * Stock's ramoops region. zumapro's bootloader keeps it across
+		 * a watchdog reset (it also writes its own log at the start of
+		 * the console zone).
+		 */
 		ramoops_reserved: ramoops@fd3ff000 {
+			compatible = "ramoops";
 			reg = <0x0 0xfd3ff000 0x00400000>;
 			no-map;
+			console-size = <0x200000>;
+			pmsg-size = <0x200000>;
 		};
 
 		/* Not in Google's list; kept reserved until shown unused. */
